From 87bceab8b1cb425422230f1c205426770e5d868e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:25:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 25/31] Read an object's placement once, from the object that
 was placed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HWP hangs a CommonObjAttr on every node of an object tree and only the
outermost one is a placement; a group's children carry defaults (왼쪽/위,
어울림, zero offsets) while their real geometry is in their render matrices.
Reading a child does not fail, it answers "top-left, in the flow", so the
same defect arrived three times in three fields and was patched three times
beside the emit site.

Placement::of is now built once and handed to everything the object emits,
at any depth. Measured on the 편람: its foreword frame is a group declaring
가운데/가운데 whose inner picture declares the defaults, so the frame had
been drawn at the paper's left edge — the page 39.6pt out. Its ink is now
symmetric (x 69.0~486.0 of 555.59pt) and its text lands at x 147.0~455.0
against rhwp's own 151~452.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
